      {
        "id": "p12-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Complete the table of values and calculate $\\dfrac{q}{\\sqrt p}$ for each pair $(q,\\sqrt p)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The $\\sqrt p$ row is $0,1,2,3,4$. The corresponding ratios are undefined, $3,3,3,3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt0&=0\\\\\\sqrt1&=1\\\\\\sqrt4&=2\\\\\\sqrt9&=3\\\\\\sqrt{16}&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $(p,q)=(0,0)$, $\\frac{q}{\\sqrt p}=\\frac{0}{0}$ is undefined. For the remaining columns:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt1}&=3\\\\\\frac{6}{\\sqrt4}&=3\\\\\\frac{9}{\\sqrt9}&=3\\\\\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{16}}&=3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Assuming that there is a simple relationship between the two variables, find a formula for $q$ in terms of $p$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$q=3\\sqrt p$.",
          "worked": "The nonzero columns have the constant ratio $\\frac{q}{\\sqrt p}=3$, so $q$ is directly proportional to $\\sqrt p$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}q&=k\\sqrt p\\\\3&=k\\sqrt1\\\\k&=3\\\\q&=3\\sqrt p\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe formula also gives $q=0$ when $p=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
